1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:07,000
Meet Apex — the Inspironics home dashboard.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Inspironics runs two complete products: the Innovation Showcase and SlidesVault.

3
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:20,600
Each had its own address, its own sign-in, and a theme that would clash with the other’s if the two were merged.

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:27,000
So Apex doesn’t merge them. It puts one small gateway in front.

5
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:32,200
One address, one port — every path goes to the right app and its API.

6
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,700
Each app still builds its own bundle, so their styles can never collide.

7
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,800
Everything starts at a single sign-in page.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,600
One email and password are checked against both platforms at once…

9
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:53,600
…and both sessions are handed to the browser, so neither app ever asks again.

10
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:59,400
The dashboard is the front door: one card per platform.

11
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:05,000
Each card probes its app live — Ready, Starting or Offline.

12
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:11,600
One account menu and one sign-out cover the dashboard and both apps.

13
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:18,200
The Innovation Showcase: 235 intelligent-infrastructure blueprints in an immersive gallery.

14
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:24,600
With a 3D ecosystem explorer, an AI copilot, offline reading and monthly PDF reports.

15
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:31,000
SlidesVault: the presentation knowledge hub for every team.

16
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:37,600
Decks sync from Dropbox, are classified with AI, and stream online or offline.

17
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:44,200
Both platforms follow one rule: the browser never talks to Dropbox.

18
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:50,600
Each API syncs, indexes and proxies every byte — no Dropbox link or token ever reaches a user.

19
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:58,200
Under the hood, the gateway has zero dependencies and one registry of every mount and port.

20
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:05,600
Every server gets its own environment, startup cleans up after itself, and a real-browser smoke test guards the integration.

21
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:12,800
Running it is one command: start.bat — the browser opens on its own.

22
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,600
start.bat prod builds and serves both apps; stop.bat stops everything Apex started.

23
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Inspironics Apex. Two platforms — one front door.
